## Verdicts (gate run 5, hack/lab/m3.sh from k3sm main @3cfade5)

- m3.0 multi-node: PASS — 2 Ready nodes (k3sm-mikostudio 100.64.0.1,
  k3sm-mikobook 100.64.1.1), worker auto-identified.
- TestM3_NodePort: PASS — cross-node NodePort round trip over the wireguard mesh.
- TestM3_InPodKubectlAndDNSOnWorker: PASS (1.05s) — the first green ever for
  this criterion (it predates the two-Mac rig and could never run honestly;
  runs 1-4 were red on three distinct now-fixed defects, below). A pod on the
  joined worker resolves kubernetes.default.svc through the in-pod DNS shim and
  completes an authenticated apiserver call over the node-local API VIP.
- TestM3_PVCPersistsAcrossRestart: RED, expected — the assertion reads pod logs,
  and every log read on this cluster fails with the kubelet serving-cert trust
  gap (`x509: certificate signed by unknown authority`, measured against the
  server node's own kubelet too). That is exactly the tracked serving-cert work
  (its branch is built and proven; merge awaits the recorded human
  merge-preconditions). Not a mesh or storage failure: the pod runs, the PVC
  binds, only the log channel is unreadable.

## Defects found by this run and FIXED live (all merged)

1. e2e test cleared the darwin nodeSelector, tripping the shipped admission
   policy (k3sm#270 — pin via hostname selector through the scheduler).
2. e2e test chained conftool through `/bin/sh -c`: dyld strips DYLD_* on exec of
   a SIP-restricted platform binary, so the DNS shim never reached conftool and
   cluster names NXDOMAINed on EVERY node (k3sm#271 — direct exec, resolve leg
   as an init container). Product-side hole filed as B243.
3. Worker staged from a home directory: the pod sandbox denies reading shim
   dylibs under /Users, dyld aborts the container (exit 134). Worked around by
   staging the dylibs into /Library/k3sm and pointing --dns-shim/--path-shim
   there; profile fix filed as B244.

## Evidence spot-checks (worker host)

- dig kubernetes.default.svc.cluster.local @10.43.0.10 -> 10.43.0.1
- curl https://10.43.0.1:443/healthz -> 401 (TLS+authn surface reached over the
